# Why this empty directory must exist in the repo.
#
# docker-compose.yml bind-mounts `./docker/postgres/data` into the
# postgres container at `/var/lib/postgresql/data`. Docker auto-creates
# missing bind-mount source directories on Linux, but only on some
# engine versions and only when the parent path is writable. On a
# fresh GitHub-hosted runner the first `docker compose up postgres`
# may fail with `source directory does not exist`.
#
# The smoke workflow (`.github/workflows/smoke.yml`) does
# `mkdir -p docker/postgres/data` before `docker compose up` to keep
# runs deterministic. This .gitkeep is the canonical in-repo proof that
# the path is expected to exist; it is intentionally the only file
# inside because postgres manages the rest at runtime.
#
# This directory is listed in `.gitignore` (we do not commit database
# data). The `.gitkeep` file is force-added by the first PR5 commit.
